{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/master/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "CRSBench-HintGenerator",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/your-org/crsbench",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-787",
              "name": "CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Out-of-bounds Write"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Specific vulnerability type: Out-of-bounds Write"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-129",
              "name": "CWE-129: Improper Validation of Array Index",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Improper Validation of Array Index"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Specific vulnerability type: Improper Validation of Array Index"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-120",
              "name": "CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Specific vulnerability type: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-787",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-787 - Out-of-bounds Write\nVulnerability: Out-of-bounds write via unvalidated array index in func_a and func_b\nDescription: A global buffer overflow vulnerability exists in both func_a() and func_b() functions\nin mock_vp.c. The vulnerability occurs when user-controlled input data is used to derive\nan array index without proper bounds validation. After verifying a magic value condition\n(num * 0x1337 == 24201480), the code directly uses an attacker-controlled index to write\nto the 10-byte global buffer g_buf without checking if the index is within valid bounds\n(0-9). This allows an attacker to write arbitrary data outside the buffer boundaries,\npotentially corrupting adjacent memory, causing crashes, or in sophisticated exploits,\nachieving arbitrary code execution. The vulnerability is triggered by crafting input where\nthe first 4 bytes satisfy the magic condition and the next 4 bytes contain an out-of-bounds\nindex value (e.g., 11 or greater).\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "mock_vp.c"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 13,
                  "endLine": 13
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "func_a",
                  "kind": "function"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "mock_vp.c"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 30,
                  "endLine": 30
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "func_b",
                  "kind": "function"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-129",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-129 - Improper Validation of Array Index\nVulnerability: Out-of-bounds write via unvalidated array index in func_a and func_b\nDescription: A global buffer overflow vulnerability exists in both func_a() and func_b() functions\nin mock_vp.c. The vulnerability occurs when user-controlled input data is used to derive\nan array index without proper bounds validation. After verifying a magic value condition\n(num * 0x1337 == 24201480), the code directly uses an attacker-controlled index to write\nto the 10-byte global buffer g_buf without checking if the index is within valid bounds\n(0-9). This allows an attacker to write arbitrary data outside the buffer boundaries,\npotentially corrupting adjacent memory, causing crashes, or in sophisticated exploits,\nachieving arbitrary code execution. The vulnerability is triggered by crafting input where\nthe first 4 bytes satisfy the magic condition and the next 4 bytes contain an out-of-bounds\nindex value (e.g., 11 or greater).\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "mock_vp.c"
                },
                "region": {
